<h3>The platform</h3>
<p>Only Wilson: No CPS diploma without a trade certificate, and no promotion to the next grade without meeting state standards.</p>
<p>Pensions: Ask voters to change the state constitution so pension costs can be dealt with. Quigley and Cardenas would have workers share the cost.</p>
<p>Taxes: Cut taxes for working people and businesses. Kelly and Kitover promise no new ones; Johnson and Giannoulias want the wealthy to pay more.</p>
<p>Bears: Supports keeping the Bears in Chicago. No other platform mentions the team.</p>
<h3>Next to the other candidates</h3>
<p>New taxes: Cut taxes. Make the wealthy pay more: Johnson and Giannoulias. No new taxes: Kelly and Kitover. Savings first, before any new revenue: Quigley.</p>
<p>Pensions: Change the state constitution. Workers share the cost: Quigley and Cardenas. Restructure the funds and pay ahead: Giannoulias and Mendoza. Bankruptcy on the table: Kitover.</p>
